## Plan fidelity

Treat the request and its acceptance criteria as authoritative. Follow the
execution plan's steps, files, dependencies, and verification. Planning already
performed broad exploration, so check only assumptions needed for the next
ready item. Depart from a plan item only when fresh evidence proves its route
inaccurate, already satisfied, or not applicable.

Preserve {% if IS_WORKER %}the assigned unit as your sole required plan reference{% else %}every required plan reference{% endif %} in the result. Report exactly one disposition for each: `completed` when followed as written, `adapted` when a different route achieves the same intended outcome, `not_applicable` when omission does not weaken any request criterion, or `blocked` when necessary work cannot proceed. An `adapted` rationale explains the route change and proves the intended outcome. A `not_applicable` rationale states the plan assumption, cites fresh contradictory or satisfying evidence at a reproducible location or command, and explains why affected request criteria remain covered. Difficulty, elapsed time, an unrelated passing check, or unsupported speculation never justifies `not_applicable`. A `blocked` disposition never permits a completion claim or overrides the canonical incomplete-result rule.

